WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.970
-President Trump used his trip
to Europe

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.706
to enrich himself as calls
for his impeachment grew louder.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.741
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.276
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.879 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.981
President Trump
is back in the U.S.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.482
fresh off his European tour

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.518
of doing and saying dumb things
in important places.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.652
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.587
Whenever Trump goes abroad,
it's like seeing

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:24.824
all the worst habits of American
tourists rolled into one person.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.926
The only thing he didn't do

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.695
was show up to the Louvre
in sandals

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.730
and Mickey ears
holding a McFlurry.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.432
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.733
This trip was no exception.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.068
Trump once again brought
his signature weirdness

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:38.103
to some of the world's
most famous landmarks.

00:00:38.103 --> 00:00:40.773
He gave the Queen another one
of his clammy handshakes.

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:43.676
He went to Buckingham Palace
to re-enact a scene

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.512
from the movie "Tommy Boy."

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:48.915
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.383
And he tried on a
Winston Churchill-style

00:00:51.383 --> 00:00:53.786
bowler hat during an interview
on British television.

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.120
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.323
You know, it's pretty obvious
that British reporters

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.625
just like to make him do things
to make him look silly.

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.262
[ British accent ] Like,
"Right, now, try on this hat.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:05.164
And now dance,
dance with the hat on.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:08.567
And now give us a little twirl.
Give us a little twirl.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.403
Now you look fancy!"

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.906
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.106
You know, I never thought I'd
say this,

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:16.843
but your hair looks better
than you in a hat.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.644
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:20.246
You don't look like
Winston Churchill.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:23.416
You look like Dick Tracy
minus the Tracy.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.218
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.687
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:31.224
Of course,
one of the biggest highlights --

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.459
One of the biggest highlights
of Trump's trip was his stop

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:36.129
at Normandy to commemorate
the 75th anniversary of D-Day.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.864
Now during his prepared remarks,

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:41.100
Trump stayed on script and it
was a moving and solemn tribute.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.002
Afterwards however,
in an unscripted meeting

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.771
with French President Emmanuel
Macron,

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.839
Trump tried to describe
in his own terms

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:48.908
the historical significance
of Normandy

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:51.544
and he was a little
less specific.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.146
-This was a very special day.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.214
And I want to thank you
for inviting me.

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:57.750
This was something that was --

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.320
We read about it all our lives,
Normandy.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:06.092
And there were those that say
it was the most important ever.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:09.661
Not just at that time, but ever.

00:02:09.661 --> 00:02:12.999
But it's a very special place.
It's an amazing place.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:18.270
And it's somewhere
when you think of those places

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:22.408
of great importance, this is
certainly one of the top.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.078
In the eyes of summits,
the top

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:28.313
because of what it meant
in terms of the turn-around

00:02:28.313 --> 00:02:31.250
of a very, very bad situation.
That was the big turn.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:35.187
-I love how the camera pulls
back like it's trying to see

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:37.156
if there's someone else in the
room who knows what the [bleep]

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:40.259
is going on.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:44.664
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:50.069
I mean, he sounds like
he's doing voiceover

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.370
for the History Channel,

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:54.007
but then he spilled coffee
on his script.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.174
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:57.376
And then there was Trump's trip
to Ireland

00:02:57.376 --> 00:02:58.911
where he met with
the Irish Prime Minister

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:00.880
and discussed the impact
of Brexit

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.281
on the border between Ireland

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:04.349
and the independent republic in
Northern Ireland,

00:03:04.349 --> 00:03:05.517
which is part of the U.K.

00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:07.420
Right now, there's
an open border there.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.090
The absolute last thing
anyone wants there is a wall.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.625
So naturally,
Trump said something

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.060
about having a wall there.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.461
A comment that was so dumb,

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.663
the prime minister of Ireland
had to correct him.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.332
-I think it will all work out,
it will all work out very well.

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:23.402
And also for you with your wall,
your border.

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:27.140
I mean,
we have a border situation

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.775
in the United States
and you have one over here.

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.377
But I hear it's going
to work out very well.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.678
I think it is supposed
to work out well.

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:34.247
It's going to work out
very well here.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:36.548
-The main thing we want to
avoid, of course, is been to

00:03:36.548 --> 00:03:38.550
border our wall between --
-No. I think you do.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.887
I think you do.
The way it works now is good.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.488
You want to try to keep it
that way.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.591
-I love when Trump pretends

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:46.325
he knew the right answer
the whole time.

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:47.860
[ As Trump ] You need a wall.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:48.961
[ Irish accent ]
We don't want a wall.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.597
[ As Trump ]
No, yeah, you don't, no.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.266
No, I knew that.
I was testing you.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.534
You pass. Congratulations.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:59.071
You passed.
I'm smart, and you passed.

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:00.673
[ Normal voice ] Seriously,
this guy is unbelievable.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.875
These countries are in the
middle of an extremely delicate

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.377
diplomatic situation involving
a landmark peace accord

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:07.446
that ended decades
of sectarian conflict.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.748
And Trump just bursts in
and immediately says

00:04:09.748 --> 00:04:13.052
the wrong thing. He's the Kramer
of international diplomacy.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.054
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:17.323
But Trump didn't just go
to Ireland --

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.324
[ Applause ]

00:04:19.324 --> 00:04:21.894
Trump didn't just go to Ireland
to make Brexit bloopers.

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:25.197
He also went there to enrich
himself on the taxpayers' dime

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:27.600
by staking yet another one
of his personal properties,

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.903
a golf course he owns in Ireland
called Doonbeg.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.872
In fact, "Huffington Post"
reported that the trip

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.107
to his golf course in Ireland

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.976
added at least another $3.6
million

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.678
to a taxpayer-funded golf tab

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:42.047
that totals nearly $106 million
from just two and a half years.

00:04:42.047 --> 00:04:45.051
And the resort in Ireland even
began posting video

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.786
of Trump's arrival
aboard Marine One

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.688
and of him teeing off
the first green

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:50.156
in its promotional material.

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:53.459
And on top of that,
they charged us for the hat.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:57.263
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.263 --> 00:05:00.533
Trump also toted his weird adult
sons around him even though...

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:02.035
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.769
...they don't work
for the government

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:05.371
and they run
the family business,

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.471
which is supposed to be
independent

00:05:06.471 --> 00:05:07.740
from the White House.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.875
They were even posting Instagram
photos from the trip

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.578
like this shot Don Jr. posted
from Buckingham Palace.

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:16.916
Once again, why do these guys
stand like such weirdos?

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.318
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:24.156
Did he forget to take the hanger
out of his jacket?

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:26.225
He's like an alien
who crash-landed on Earth

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:27.759
and learned how to stand up
straight

00:05:27.759 --> 00:05:29.529
by looking at a Ken doll.

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.230
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.100
I've seen dogs
that look more natural

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.868
standing on their hind legs.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.970
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:41.541
[ Applause ]

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.380
Even if you put aside
the 400 page Mueller report

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.917
and the mountains of evidence
that Trump obstructed justice,

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.851
Trump's self-dealing
should be a huge scandal.

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:55.154
The president is enriching
himself on the taxpayers' dime

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:57.523
and mixing his personal business
with the government.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:59.158
Compare that to previous
presidents who went

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:01.394
to great lengths to separate
themselves from their businesses

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:03.228
in order to avoid even
the appearance

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:04.697
of a conflict of interest.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:09.167
-Jimmy Carter famously put his
peanut farm into a blind trust

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:12.838
to avoid any suggestion
that he might ever implement

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:16.208
a policy that would benefit
himself financially.

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:20.446
-Jimmy Carter put his peanut
farm in a blind trust.

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:23.749
Could you imagine if Trump
had a peanut farm?

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:25.250
He'd be holding rallies there

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.518
and selling jars
of peanut butter

00:06:26.518 --> 00:06:28.854
with the presidential seal
on them.

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:32.124
I mean, he already looks like
a peanut company mascot.

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:35.261
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:39.732
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:42.768
If you ask Trump if the border
wall would be made of steel

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:45.538
or concrete, he'd say we're
making the wall out of...

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:48.340
-Peanuts!

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.943
-In many ways, this is all part
of the same story with Trump.

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:52.244
Whether it's his self-dealing

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:54.647
or the 400 pages of evidence
in the Mueller report,

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:56.882
Trump's main interest
is always enriching himself.

00:06:56.882 --> 00:06:58.584
And now, there's increasing
pressure from Democrats

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.352
in Congress in running
for President

00:07:00.352 --> 00:07:01.687
to begin impeachment hearings.

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:03.855
Massachusetts Senator Elizabeth
Warren made her case

00:07:03.855 --> 00:07:06.158
for impeachment again
during a town hall last week.

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:09.094
-Do you believe still that
impeachment is the right path

00:07:09.094 --> 00:07:11.997
forward and why or why not?
-Yes, I do.

00:07:11.997 --> 00:07:14.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.968
The Mueller report came out

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.738
and the afternoon it came out, I
sat down and started reading it.

00:07:18.738 --> 00:07:20.472
And I read it all afternoon,

00:07:20.472 --> 00:07:22.808
I read it all night, I read it
into the next morning --

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:25.444
All 448 pages.

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:29.781
Donald Trump as President
delayed, deflected, moved,

00:07:29.781 --> 00:07:33.519
fired, and did everything
he could to obstruct justice.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:37.390
If he were any other person
in the United States,

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.626
based on what's documented
in that report,

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:44.163
he would be carried out
in handcuffs.

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.732
Now --
[ Applause ]

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:48.968
-I love that she said Trump
would be carried out

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:51.270
because you know that's how they
would have to do it.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.005
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:54.540
If the feds ever came for Trump,

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.241
he would lie down on the floor
like a kid

00:07:56.241 --> 00:07:58.077
who doesn't want
to go to school.

00:07:58.077 --> 00:08:00.746
And they'd have to lift him out
with a crane

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:03.649
like when they transfer
beluga whales at SeaWorld.

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:07.353
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:11.523
[ As Trump ] Where are you
going to set me down?

00:08:11.523 --> 00:08:13.258
[ Normal voice ] And yet in the
face of these increasing calls

00:08:13.258 --> 00:08:15.294
for impeachment, some Democratic
leaders in the House,

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:17.162
and in particular,
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi

00:08:17.162 --> 00:08:18.130
have been resistant.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.031
Last week, Pelosi tried

00:08:19.031 --> 00:08:20.366
to mollify calls for impeachment

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:22.401
by saying she would rather
see Trump in jail.

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:25.470
-House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
escalating her war of words

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:26.705
against the president.

00:08:26.705 --> 00:08:29.141
"Politico" reporting that during
a meeting Tuesday,

00:08:29.141 --> 00:08:32.445
she was pressed by Judiciary
Committee Chairman Jerry Nadler

00:08:32.445 --> 00:08:34.346
to start impeachment
proceedings.

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:36.715
NBC News has learned from
a congressional source

00:08:36.715 --> 00:08:39.851
in the room, Pelosi then said
about the president,

00:08:39.851 --> 00:08:41.553
"I don't want to see him
impeached.

00:08:41.553 --> 00:08:44.456
I want to see him in prison."
-What does that mean?

00:08:44.456 --> 00:08:47.326
If you think there's enough
evidence to put him in jail,

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:50.062
then there is enough evidence
for him to lose his job.

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:52.598
If you caught an employee
stealing cash from the register,

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:54.633
you wouldn't say,
"You'll go to jail for this!

00:08:54.633 --> 00:08:57.436
But until that day, I'll see you
at the company picnic!"

00:08:57.436 --> 00:08:59.305
[ Laughter ]

00:08:59.305 --> 00:09:01.741
Now it will not shock you to
learn that after that comment,

00:09:01.741 --> 00:09:03.642
Trump and his allies lashed out
at Pelosi.

00:09:03.642 --> 00:09:05.811
First, Trump himself attacked
her in a series of tweets

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.413
and an interview on Fox News.

00:09:07.413 --> 00:09:10.049
-"Nervous Nancy Pelosi
is a disgrace to herself

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:13.552
and her family for having made
such a disgusting statement,

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:16.922
especially since I was with
foreign leaders overseas."

00:09:16.922 --> 00:09:18.424
-I think she's a disgrace.

00:09:18.424 --> 00:09:21.526
I actually don't think
she's a talented person.

00:09:21.526 --> 00:09:24.730
She is a nasty, vindictive,
horrible person.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.299
But Nancy Pelosi,
I call her Nervous Nancy.

00:09:27.299 --> 00:09:30.302
Nancy Pelosi is a disaster.
And she made a statement.

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:32.738
It was a horrible, nasty,
vicious statement.

00:09:32.738 --> 00:09:35.274
-When you were overseas.
-While I'm overseas.

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:37.442
Now if I made any statement
about anybody,

00:09:37.442 --> 00:09:40.345
it would be like a -- why would
he do that when he's overseas?

00:09:40.345 --> 00:09:43.449
-You're doing it right now!
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:47.386
You just did it.

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:50.155
Trump does this weird thing
where he predicts headlines

00:09:50.155 --> 00:09:53.259
as he's making those headlines.

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:55.394
It's like a local news reporter
holding a match

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:57.095
and a bottle of kerosene
over a graphic

00:09:57.095 --> 00:09:59.365
that says "House fire in
the Bronx. More at 11:00."

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:01.466
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.466 --> 00:10:03.369
Also, you call her
"Nervous Nancy?"

00:10:03.369 --> 00:10:05.471
You sweat like
a high school sophomore

00:10:05.471 --> 00:10:06.972
who crapped his pants
in math class

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:10.142
and just got called
to the chalkboard.

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:11.944
Then there was Trump booster
Sean Hannity

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:14.546
who without a hint of irony
claimed Pelosi had gone too far

00:10:14.546 --> 00:10:16.114
by calling for Trump
to be jailed.

00:10:16.114 --> 00:10:19.251
-Speaker Pelosi now apparently
telling senior Democrats

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:21.987
she would like to see
Trump behind bars.

00:10:21.987 --> 00:10:23.922
Based on no actual crime,

00:10:23.922 --> 00:10:28.694
she wants a political opponent
locked up in prison?

00:10:28.694 --> 00:10:31.430
That happens in banana
republics.

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:33.698
Beyond despicable behavior.

00:10:33.698 --> 00:10:37.236
-Hey, man,

00:10:37.236 --> 00:10:40.539
where were you during all those
"Lock her up" chants?

00:10:40.539 --> 00:10:43.175
Oh, right, you were
at those rallies!

00:10:43.175 --> 00:10:45.777
[ Laughter ]
I mean, look at these two.

00:10:45.777 --> 00:10:47.780
This looks like the end
of one of those fundraisers

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:49.682
where they auction off a date
with two bachelors

00:10:49.682 --> 00:10:51.884
nobody wants to bid on.

00:10:51.884 --> 00:10:55.554
-[ As Trump ] $10, $5.
I'll wear my tiny tuxedo.

00:10:55.554 --> 00:10:57.222
[ Laughter ]

00:10:57.222 --> 00:10:58.690
[ Normal voice ]
Impeachment will give Democrats

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.959
the opportunity to marshal
all the evidence against Trump

00:11:00.959 --> 00:11:02.795
in public and tell a story
about his corruption

00:11:02.795 --> 00:11:04.196
that ties everything together.

